.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH ckman-config-ndef 1  ckman 
.SH NAME
ckman\-config\-ndef \- Read or replace the NDEF message
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBckman\-config\-ndef\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Read or replace the NDEF message.
.PP
Writes are crash\-consistent: a crash or unplug mid\-write leaves an empty message instead of a partially written one.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
ckman\-config\-ndef\-read(1)
Read the stored NDEF message
.TP
ckman\-config\-ndef\-write(1)
Replace the NDEF message with the file contents (\*(Aq\-\*(Aq for stdin)
.TP
ckman\-config\-ndef\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
